  "areas": {
    "about": "Areas (Anthony, 30 October 2026). Ozi Delivery runs across the whole UK, and every area is open: nobody is ever refused because of where they are. An area is a UK postcode area, the letters a postcode starts with; an area missing from 'names' is called by its letters. 'groups' are areas run as one: the London postcode areas are one area, London. Areas are kept for staff to see and for sending jobs to local Runners, same area, nearest first; staff can pause one. 'openWords' is what a Shopper asking about an area is told ({area} is its name). 'noRunnerWords' is the gentle warning given only as a Shopper places an order, on the confirmation screen, by voice and on the telephone, when their delivery area has no approved Runner able to work yet or is paused; it never stops the order. 'goAheadQuestion' is asked after it by voice and on the telephone, and 'noRunnerOkButton' and 'noRunnerShareButton' are its two buttons on the screen. 'inviteDriverWords' goes with the Shopper's referral link to a driver ({link} is the link). 'runnerJoinedWords' is the one text a warned Shopper gets when a Runner is approved in their area, never sent between 'textQuietFrom' and 'textQuietUntil' (UK time). 'statusHasRunner', 'statusNoRunner' and 'statusPaused' are the status words on the staff Areas page. A Runner's live position older than 'livePositionMinutes' is not trusted, and their home postcode is used. The Runner app shares where they are every 'shareOnShiftSeconds' while on shift, and every 'shareOnJobSeconds' at most while they have a job in hand.",
